<BaseLayout title="Editorial Standards | B Tecky" description="How B Tecky researches, reviews, updates and corrects technology guides and opportunity announcements.">
<main class="editorial-page">
<section class="editorial-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">HOW WE WORK</p><h1 class="display">Editorial standards</h1><p>Our commitment is to publish useful, understandable technology learning resources and clearly labelled opportunity information—not pages created only to attract clicks.</p><small>Policy established: 6 November 2026</small></div></section>
<article class="container editorial-content">
<section><h2>Our purpose</h2><p>B Tecky publishes practical explainers, tutorials, project guidance, technology analysis and selected community opportunities. We aim to help readers understand a topic, make a better decision or take a useful next step.</p></section>
<section><h2>Research and sources</h2><p>For product announcements, program rules, deadlines, eligibility and other changing information, we prioritize the original vendor, organizer, employer, standards body or official documentation. Secondary sources may provide context, but they do not replace primary evidence for material claims. Readers should follow the linked official source for the latest terms.</p></section>
<section><h2>Practical accuracy</h2><p>Technical examples should identify relevant versions and assumptions where they affect the result. Code and commands should be reviewed for clarity and tested in a suitable environment when practical. Articles should explain limitations, trade-offs and failure cases—not present a demo as proof of production readiness.</p></section>
<section><h2>AI assistance and human responsibility</h2><p>Digital tools, including AI-assisted tools, may support research, outlining or editing. They do not replace editorial responsibility. A human editor is responsible for reviewing claims, checking sources, removing unsupported statements and deciding whether a page is useful enough to publish. We do not treat automated text generation or word count as evidence of quality.</p></section>
<section><h2>Opportunity announcements</h2><p>Events, internships, challenges, scholarships, giveaways and reward programs are labelled separately from evergreen technical guides. Such information can change or expire. We aim to state eligibility, deadlines, geography, selection criteria, reward conditions and official links when those details are available. Participation does not guarantee selection, employment, certification or rewards. Always confirm current details with the organizer.</p></section>
<section><h2>Updates and corrections</h2><p>We update articles when important facts, software versions, links or program terms change. A displayed update date should represent a substantive review, not a cosmetic edit. If you find an error, outdated information or a broken example, please <a href="/contact?subject=Editorial%20correction">send an editorial correction</a> with the article URL and supporting evidence. We review corrections and update pages when warranted.</p></section>
<section><h2>Authorship and independence</h2><p>B Tecky is an independent creator-led publication. Author information appears on article pages and our <a href="/about/">About page</a>. Product names, company names and trademarks belong to their respective owners. Unless explicitly stated, B Tecky is not affiliated with or endorsed by the organizations discussed.</p></section>
<section><h2>Advertising and reader trust</h2><p>Advertising, where present, is separate from editorial decisions. Advertisers do not determine our explanations, conclusions or recommendations. We aim to keep navigation clear and the main content useful, accessible and easy to distinguish from promotional material.</p></section>
<section><h2>Contact</h2><p>Questions about these standards or a specific article can be sent through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p></section>
</article></main>
